# Go Style Rules

## General
- Go version: 1.22+
- Module path: github.com/ctxlite/ctxlite
- Return all errors explicitly; never ignore with `_`
- Do not use `panic()` outside `main.go` startup validation
- Prefer `errors.New()` and `fmt.Errorf("context: %w", err)` for error wrapping

## Naming
- Package names: lowercase, single word (e.g. `proxy`, `cache`, `trimmer`, `mcp`, `stats`)
- Interfaces: `-er` suffix when appropriate (e.g. `Cacher`, `Trimmer`)
- Exported functions: PascalCase
- Internal helpers: camelCase
- Constants: ALL_CAPS only for sentinel errors, otherwise PascalCase

## Structure
- Each package has a `doc.go` file with the package comment
- Constructors follow `New<Type>(config Config) (*Type, error)`
- Cleanup via `io.Closer` interface, not custom methods

## HTTP
- ALWAYS bind on `127.0.0.1`, never on `0.0.0.0`
- Mandatory timeouts on any `http.Server`: ReadTimeout, WriteTimeout, IdleTimeout
- Never log Authorization headers or API keys

## Logging
- Use `log/slog` (stdlib, Go 1.21+)
- Default level: `INFO`
- Format: text on stderr (not JSON in v1)
- Never log request body or response body — they may contain sensitive data

## Testing
- Each package has a `*_test.go` file
- Use stdlib `testing`, no external frameworks
- Table-driven tests for cache and trimming logic
